WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.428 --> 00:00:03.512
Unit eleven. Physical Activity Guidelines!

2
00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:08.129
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:11.106
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.156 --> 00:00:15.164
Today we learn about Physical Activity Guidelines. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:20.207
Physical activity. Say it with me. Physical activity!

6
00:00:23.715 --> 00:00:27.149
Aerobic. Say it with me. Aerobic!

7
00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:33.623
Strength. Say it with me. Strength!

8
00:00:37.099 --> 00:00:41.133
60 minutes. Say it with me. 60 minutes!

9
00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:47.909
Heart rate. Say it with me. Heart rate!

10
00:00:51.377 --> 00:00:54.327
Sitting. Say it with me. Sitting!

11
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.044
Sport. Say it with me. Sport!

12
00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:07.794
Fitness. Say it with me. Fitness!

13
00:01:11.289 --> 00:01:22.247
Teenagers should get about 60 minutes of physical activity daily, mostly aerobic. Strength activities should be included at least three days a week. Reducing long sitting time also improves fitness.

14
00:01:22.297 --> 00:01:25.049
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:26.306 --> 00:01:31.528
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:31.578 --> 00:01:32.728
Strength!

17
00:01:33.446 --> 00:01:38.504
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:39.704
Sport!

19
00:01:40.623 --> 00:01:46.407
Did you know? The WHO recommends muscle- and bone-strengthening activities at least 3 days a week for young people!

20
00:01:46.457 --> 00:01:48.263
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:49.705 --> 00:01:57.029
Think and answer. Which activities raise your heart rate?

22
00:01:57.079 --> 00:01:58.229
Great answer!

23
00:01:59.206 --> 00:02:03.694
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:03.744 --> 00:02:06.254
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

